WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.292
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Cambridge exams.

2
00:00:05.592 --> 00:00:09.037
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.337 --> 00:00:18.200
Unit ten: B1 Preliminary: Speaking. Today you will talk about yourself, describe a photo and discuss a situation with a partner.

4
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:21.071
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:22.033 --> 00:00:25.289
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:27.151
Describe.

7
00:00:28.150 --> 00:00:30.614
Describe means to say what something is like.

8
00:00:31.217 --> 00:00:32.694
Describe the photo.

9
00:00:33.283 --> 00:00:36.017
Your turn. Say: Describe.

10
00:00:38.867 --> 00:00:39.763
Describe.

11
00:00:40.517 --> 00:00:41.599
Background.

12
00:00:42.583 --> 00:00:45.721
Background means the part of a picture behind the main subject.

13
00:00:46.317 --> 00:00:48.200
In the background there is a tree.

14
00:00:48.817 --> 00:00:51.097
Your turn. Say: Background.

15
00:00:53.933 --> 00:00:55.097
Background.

16
00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:56.689
Foreground.

17
00:00:57.683 --> 00:00:59.706
Foreground means the part near the front.

18
00:01:00.317 --> 00:01:02.130
In the foreground there is a girl.

19
00:01:02.717 --> 00:01:05.427
Your turn. Say: Foreground.

20
00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:09.198
Foreground.

21
00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:10.835
Probably.

22
00:01:11.850 --> 00:01:14.848
Probably means used when you are fairly sure.

23
00:01:15.450 --> 00:01:17.032
They are probably friends.

24
00:01:17.617 --> 00:01:20.072
Your turn. Say: Probably.

25
00:01:22.933 --> 00:01:23.865
Probably.

26
00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:25.711
Looks like.

27
00:01:26.717 --> 00:01:29.146
Looks like means seems similar to.

28
00:01:29.750 --> 00:01:31.239
It looks like a market.

29
00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:34.305
Your turn. Say: Looks like.

30
00:01:37.167 --> 00:01:38.214
Looks like.

31
00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:39.847
Agree.

32
00:01:40.850 --> 00:01:42.838
Agree means to share an opinion.

33
00:01:43.450 --> 00:01:44.718
I agree with you.

34
00:01:45.317 --> 00:01:47.516
Your turn. Say: Agree.

35
00:01:50.367 --> 00:01:51.275
Agree.

36
00:01:52.017 --> 00:01:53.099
Suggest.

37
00:01:54.083 --> 00:01:56.083
Suggest means to give an idea.

38
00:01:56.683 --> 00:01:58.381
I suggest the museum.

39
00:01:58.983 --> 00:02:01.415
Your turn. Say: Suggest.

40
00:02:04.267 --> 00:02:05.221
Suggest.

41
00:02:05.983 --> 00:02:06.833
Decision.

42
00:02:07.850 --> 00:02:09.722
Decision means a choice you make.

43
00:02:10.317 --> 00:02:12.096
We made a decision together.

44
00:02:12.683 --> 00:02:15.475
Your turn. Say: Decision.

45
00:02:18.333 --> 00:02:19.276
Decision.

46
00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:23.485
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:26.826
Visal, what are the four Speaking parts?

48
00:02:27.917 --> 00:02:41.766
First, the examiner asks you about your life. Second, you discuss a situation with your partner. Third, you describe a photo for a minute. Finally, you talk about a related topic together.

49
00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:44.466
How do I describe a photo?

50
00:02:45.550 --> 00:02:54.135
Say where the people are, what they are doing and how they feel. Use phrases such as in the foreground, in the background and it looks like.

51
00:02:55.250 --> 00:02:57.238
How do I discuss with a partner?

52
00:02:58.350 --> 00:03:07.478
Give your idea, ask your partner for an opinion, agree or disagree politely and try to reach a decision together.

53
00:03:08.633 --> 00:03:10.319
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:11.183 --> 00:03:15.389
Grammar focus: Strategy: describe, suggest, agree.

55
00:03:15.689 --> 00:03:16.887
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:17.583 --> 00:03:20.024
In the foreground there is a girl holding a bag.

57
00:03:20.917 --> 00:03:23.615
I suggest the museum. What do you think?

58
00:03:24.567 --> 00:03:31.608
Use clear language to describe photos and discuss with your partner. Ask questions, agree politely and speak naturally.

59
00:03:32.350 --> 00:03:35.838
Be careful! Don't say: I only say yes or no.

60
00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.682
Say: I give reasons and ask questions.

61
00:03:40.982 --> 00:03:42.401
Speak and interact.

62
00:03:43.200 --> 00:03:46.433
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

63
00:03:47.233 --> 00:03:48.676
Describing a Photo.

64
00:03:48.976 --> 00:03:51.231
Rattana describes a photo of a market.

65
00:03:52.233 --> 00:03:54.918
In the foreground there is a woman selling fruit.

66
00:03:55.933 --> 00:03:58.235
In the background there are colourful umbrellas.

67
00:03:59.233 --> 00:04:02.208
It looks like a busy morning and the people seem happy.

68
00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:05.722
She ends by saying she would like to visit it.

69
00:04:06.833 --> 00:04:10.464
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

70
00:04:11.317 --> 00:04:13.235
In Part 3 you blank a photo.

71
00:04:13.535 --> 00:04:16.724
A, delete. B, describe. C, draw.

72
00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:22.452
The answer is B: describe.

73
00:04:23.617 --> 00:04:25.407
'In the foreground' means blank.

74
00:04:25.707 --> 00:04:30.022
A, far away. B, behind a wall. C, near the front.

75
00:04:33.567 --> 00:04:35.891
The answer is C: near the front.

76
00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:39.607
A good phrase to ask your partner is blank.

77
00:04:39.907 --> 00:04:43.978
A, What do you think?. B, Be quiet.. C, Go away..

78
00:04:47.533 --> 00:04:49.684
The answer is A: What do you think?.

79
00:04:50.850 --> 00:04:52.362
What does the woman sell?

80
00:04:52.662 --> 00:04:55.990
A, books. B, fruit. C, cars.

81
00:04:59.533 --> 00:05:01.208
The answer is B: fruit.

82
00:05:02.350 --> 00:05:04.338
The speakers should try to reach blank.

83
00:05:04.638 --> 00:05:09.383
A, an argument. B, silence. C, a decision.

84
00:05:12.933 --> 00:05:14.944
The answer is C: a decision.

85
00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:19.157
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

86
00:05:20.017 --> 00:05:22.190
How do you describe a photo in Speaking?

87
00:05:30.983 --> 00:05:32.518
Now listen to Visal.

88
00:05:32.818 --> 00:05:46.538
I say where the people are and what they are doing, and I use phrases like in the foreground and in the background. I also talk about how they look and feel. If I am not sure about something, I use looks like or probably.

89
00:05:46.838 --> 00:05:48.663
Excellent answer, Visal!

90
00:05:49.550 --> 00:05:54.884
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and strategy: describe, suggest, agree.

91
00:05:55.184 --> 00:05:59.218
Today's value is confidence. Speak up and be proud of who you are.

92
00:05:59.518 --> 00:06:02.031
See you in Unit eleven. Goodbye!

93
00:06:02.331 --> 00:06:04.763
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

